Routes the OV08X40 through the CVS bridge in the IPU75XA sensor graph, as
Intel's own commit f167239 does for the IPU8 graph, since Linux 7.2 puts the
bridge between the sensor and the IPU.

From nixos-hardware PR #1912 at 7ea3467 (dell/xps/14-da14260/ipu7-camera-hal/
ipu75xa-ov08x40-cvs.patch), matching the configuration Omarchy runs on this
laptop.

--- a/config/linux/ipu75xa/sensors/ov08x40-uf.json
+++ b/config/linux/ipu75xa/sensors/ov08x40-uf.json
@@ -32,13 +32,25 @@
                 "format": "V4L2_MBUS_FMT_SGRBG10_1X10"
               },
               {
+                "name": "Intel CVS", "pad": 0, "width": 3856, "height": 2176,
+                "format": "V4L2_MBUS_FMT_SGRBG10_1X10"
+              },
+              {
+                "name": "Intel CVS", "pad": 1, "width": 3856, "height": 2176,
+                "format": "V4L2_MBUS_FMT_SGRBG10_1X10"
+              },
+              {
                 "name": "Intel IPU7 CSI2 $CSI_PORT", "pad": 0, "width": 3856, "height": 2176,
                 "format": "V4L2_MBUS_FMT_SGRBG10_1X10"
               }
             ],
             "link": [
               {
-                "srcName": "ov08x40 $I2CBUS", "srcPad": 0, "sinkName": "Intel IPU7 CSI2 $CSI_PORT",
+                "srcName": "ov08x40 $I2CBUS", "srcPad": 0, "sinkName": "Intel CVS",
+                "sinkPad": 0, "enable": true
+              },
+              {
+                "srcName": "Intel CVS", "srcPad": 1, "sinkName": "Intel IPU7 CSI2 $CSI_PORT",
                 "sinkPad": 0, "enable": true
               },
               {
